WEBVTT

00:00:33.619 --> 00:00:36.719
have tripped every speedtrap in Smolville to get here. What happened?

00:00:36.719 --> 00:00:39.219
I got another SOS from Kara.

00:00:39.219 --> 00:00:40.920
And?

00:00:40.920 --> 00:00:48.020
Krypton will be destroyed any minute. Brainiac is getting closer, please hurry.

00:00:48.020 --> 00:00:51.119
Your life depends on it.

00:00:51.119 --> 00:00:57.320
So Brainiac used Kara to time jump back to the day that the planet exploded.

00:00:57.320 --> 00:01:04.989
Which means that all he has to do is stop that ship that carried you as a baby from leaving Krypton and...

00:01:04.989 --> 00:01:06.989
You'd be standing alone in empty day.

00:01:06.989 --> 00:01:07.989
An empty barn.

00:01:07.989 --> 00:01:14.579
Clark, if they made the quantum leap, there must be a way you can too.

00:01:14.579 --> 00:01:16.579
Yeah.

00:01:16.579 --> 00:01:19.579
Kara mentioned the fortress has the ability to send me back.

00:01:19.579 --> 00:01:22.579
If I take the octagonal disc there, Jarrell can make it happen.

00:01:22.579 --> 00:01:27.840
Then why are you still here?

00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:30.840
I mean, you should be halfway to Krypton by now.

00:01:30.840 --> 00:01:36.560
I'm not going.

00:01:36.560 --> 00:01:38.560
But you have to stop Brainiac or you'll fade away.

00:01:38.560 --> 00:01:40.560
I mean, this could happen at any moment.

00:01:40.560 --> 00:01:41.560
I understand that.

00:01:41.560 --> 00:01:43.560
Okay, I know what you're thinking, Clark.

00:01:43.560 --> 00:01:45.560
The last time you meddled with the past, it cost your father's life.

00:01:45.560 --> 00:01:47.560
father is life, but Clark, look at what's at stake.

00:01:47.560 --> 00:01:49.560
You don't have a choice.

00:01:49.560 --> 00:01:50.560
I do have a choice, Chloe.

00:01:50.560 --> 00:01:51.560
I'm making it right now.

00:01:51.560 --> 00:01:54.560
Ever since I arrived, all I brought is death and suffering.

00:01:54.560 --> 00:01:58.560
Meteor freaks, phantoms, or Brainiac.

00:01:58.560 --> 00:02:02.560
Clark, you've done so much good.

00:02:02.560 --> 00:02:05.560
You can't blame yourself for all the bad in the world.

00:02:05.560 --> 00:02:07.560
It's not blame, Chloe.

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:11.560
I'm taking responsibility for all the lives that I've ruined,

00:02:11.560 --> 00:02:13.560
including Lana's.

00:02:13.560 --> 00:02:14.560
Clark, this is not the time to be seen.

00:02:14.560 --> 00:02:16.560
It's not the time to be stubborn, okay?

00:02:16.560 --> 00:02:17.560
Don't do this.

00:02:17.560 --> 00:02:18.560
We need you.

00:02:18.560 --> 00:02:20.560
I need you.

00:02:20.560 --> 00:02:22.560
Chloe, you'll be fine.

00:02:22.560 --> 00:02:25.560
Once I'm gone, you'll have no idea I was ever here.

00:02:25.560 --> 00:02:26.560
No!

00:02:26.560 --> 00:02:27.560
I'm not letting you off that easy.

00:02:27.560 --> 00:02:29.560
You're going back to Krypton now.

00:02:29.560 --> 00:02:31.560
Before it's too late.

00:02:31.560 --> 00:02:34.560
This planet will be better off if I never existed.

00:02:34.560 --> 00:03:05.479
Oh my God, Clark.

00:03:05.479 --> 00:03:14.740
Chloe!

00:03:14.740 --> 00:03:17.740
Hey! What the hell are you doing on our property?

00:03:17.740 --> 00:03:23.780
What? Who are you?

00:03:23.780 --> 00:03:24.780
Who are you?

00:03:24.780 --> 00:03:30.680
I live here.

00:03:30.680 --> 00:03:31.680
I'm Clark Kent.

00:03:31.680 --> 00:04:49.449
I'm not in this picture.

00:04:49.449 --> 00:04:50.449
You're their son.

00:04:50.449 --> 00:04:51.449
Yeah.

00:04:51.449 --> 00:04:54.449
And lucky for you, my dad didn't find you in the barn.

00:04:54.449 --> 00:04:57.449
Does he be pulling on his 12-gauge right about now?

00:04:57.449 --> 00:04:58.449
He's alive?

00:04:58.449 --> 00:05:06.120
Dad? What's your problem?

00:05:06.120 --> 00:05:07.120
Look, nobody's home, alright?

00:05:07.120 --> 00:05:10.120
If you don't get out of my house, I'm calling the sheriff.

00:05:10.120 --> 00:05:13.120
I never made to earth. I don't exist here.

00:05:13.120 --> 00:05:17.120
Well, unfortunately, you do, and you still haven't told me why you're in my house.

00:05:17.120 --> 00:05:18.120
I'm not sure.

00:05:18.120 --> 00:05:20.120
If I didn't get on that ship, then I shouldn't be here, but somehow I

00:05:20.120 --> 00:05:21.120
I am.

00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:22.120
The ship?

00:05:22.120 --> 00:05:26.399
Look, just relax, okay?

00:05:26.399 --> 00:05:28.399
I'll get you some help.

00:05:28.399 --> 00:05:30.399
I need to talk to Jonathan and Martha.

00:05:30.399 --> 00:05:34.399
Well, that's gonna be hard, because they're on a crew celebrating my dad's birthday.

00:05:34.399 --> 00:05:35.399
Look, anyways...

00:05:35.399 --> 00:05:37.399
I don't know who that is.

00:05:37.399 --> 00:05:41.399
I don't know who that is, but I'll call the sheriff,

00:05:41.399 --> 00:05:42.399
and I'm sure he'll know what to do.

00:05:42.399 --> 00:05:43.399
No, it's all right.

00:05:43.399 --> 00:05:46.899
I just need to make sure all my friends are okay.

00:05:46.899 --> 00:06:08.069
I need to use your phone book.

00:06:08.069 --> 00:06:09.069
I'll be right back now.

00:06:09.069 --> 00:06:11.069
Okay, I'll be waiting for you.

00:06:11.069 --> 00:06:21.279
Chloe.

00:06:21.279 --> 00:06:26.240
Hey, Chloe Sullivan, Smallville High, Class V.

00:06:26.240 --> 00:06:30.240
I'm sorry my inner database is coming up empty.

00:06:30.240 --> 00:06:32.240
Do I know you?

00:06:32.240 --> 00:06:35.240
Clark Kent?

00:06:35.240 --> 00:06:37.240
We went to high school together.

00:06:37.240 --> 00:06:43.920
You may not remember me. I was a bit of an outsider.

00:06:43.920 --> 00:06:46.920
Listen, I'm trying to find a mutual friend of ours.

00:06:46.920 --> 00:06:50.389
She's not in the phone book. Lana Lang?

00:06:50.389 --> 00:06:52.389
The cheerleader?

00:06:52.389 --> 00:06:55.389
We didn't exactly swim in the same social ponds.

00:06:55.389 --> 00:06:57.389
I mean, to be honest, her blift fell off my reader the day.

00:06:57.389 --> 00:06:59.389
I fell off my radar the day after graduation.

00:06:59.389 --> 00:07:02.639
But you were a report at the torch, right?

00:07:02.639 --> 00:07:04.639
Maybe you can use some of your investigative magic.

00:07:04.639 --> 00:07:06.639
Help me track her down.

00:07:06.639 --> 00:07:10.639
I would love to help, but we have someone we have to be.

00:07:10.639 --> 00:07:13.639
Oh, you're, you and your boyfriend.

00:07:13.639 --> 00:07:15.639
Fiancee, actually.

00:07:15.639 --> 00:07:17.639
Weddings on Sunday.

00:07:17.639 --> 00:07:22.519
Congratulations.

00:07:22.519 --> 00:07:26.399
That's great.

00:07:26.399 --> 00:07:28.399
So you ready?

00:07:28.399 --> 00:07:29.399
Yeah.

00:07:29.399 --> 00:07:30.399
Your dad just called.

00:07:30.399 --> 00:07:31.399
He's waiting at the tuxedo shop.

00:07:31.399 --> 00:07:32.399
Okay.

00:07:32.399 --> 00:07:35.399
I'm sorry I couldn't help.

00:07:35.399 --> 00:07:36.399
It's okay.

00:07:36.399 --> 00:07:37.399
Ready?

00:07:37.399 --> 00:07:38.399
I hope you find Lana.

00:07:38.399 --> 00:07:41.930
Chloe.

00:07:41.930 --> 00:07:43.930
I'm really happy for you.

00:07:43.930 --> 00:07:46.819
Thanks.

00:07:46.819 --> 00:07:50.360
Nice bow tie.

00:07:50.360 --> 00:08:02.560
Oh, thanks.

00:08:02.560 --> 00:08:15.540
Yeah, it's a present from an old girlfriend.

00:08:15.540 --> 00:08:19.540
Oh, thanks. Yeah, it's a present from an old girlfriend.

00:08:19.540 --> 00:08:23.540
She might have taken my heart away, but she left him with a sense of style.

00:08:23.540 --> 00:08:26.540
You're Jimmy Olson. The photographer, right?

00:08:26.540 --> 00:08:28.540
The one and only.

00:08:28.540 --> 00:08:29.540
Every time I see a picture in the need.

00:08:29.540 --> 00:08:32.539
newspaper I like, your name's on it.

00:08:32.539 --> 00:08:33.539
Really?

00:08:33.539 --> 00:08:35.539
You like my work?

00:08:35.539 --> 00:08:36.539
Yeah.

00:08:36.539 --> 00:08:37.539
I wish that you were my editor.

00:08:37.539 --> 00:08:39.539
I mean, she says that I have focus issues.

00:08:39.539 --> 00:08:41.539
She should check her eyesight.

00:08:41.539 --> 00:08:44.539
So, do you work here?

00:08:44.539 --> 00:08:45.539
No.

00:08:45.539 --> 00:08:49.539
I actually lost track of my ex-girlfriend.

00:08:49.539 --> 00:08:51.539
I was hoping the Daily Planet Archives

00:08:51.539 --> 00:08:53.539
might help me find out where she ended up.

00:08:53.539 --> 00:08:56.539
Do you have any idea who might be able to help me?

00:08:56.539 --> 00:08:57.539
You're looking at them?

00:08:57.539 --> 00:08:58.539
I was there for a loyal fan.

00:08:58.539 --> 00:08:59.539
I was there for a loyal fan.

00:08:59.539 --> 00:09:00.539
Come on.

00:09:00.539 --> 00:09:11.090
So, does this long-lost love have a name?

00:09:11.090 --> 00:09:12.090
Lana Lang.

00:09:12.090 --> 00:09:13.090
Lana Lang.

00:09:13.090 --> 00:09:19.370
Lana Lang.

00:09:19.370 --> 00:09:22.320
Uh-oh.

00:09:22.320 --> 00:09:24.320
What is it? Is she okay?

00:09:24.320 --> 00:09:26.320
I'll brace yourself.

00:09:26.320 --> 00:09:29.320
After high school, Lana Lang studied art history at the Sobeau,

00:09:29.320 --> 00:09:31.320
where she met French philanthropist Pierre Rousseau.

00:09:31.320 --> 00:09:35.320
Like, they're married, they have two kids, and they live in the city of lights.

00:09:35.320 --> 00:09:37.320
Sorry, buddy.

00:09:37.320 --> 00:09:40.320
No, it's the best news I ever heard.

00:09:40.320 --> 00:09:41.320
Really?

00:09:41.320 --> 00:09:43.320
I guess things turned out pretty good for me.

00:09:43.320 --> 00:09:45.320
It turned out pretty good for her without your round.

00:09:45.320 --> 00:09:51.259
I just wanted to be happy.

00:09:51.259 --> 00:09:52.259
Thanks.

00:09:52.259 --> 00:09:58.549
Humsy, but cute.

00:09:58.549 --> 00:10:04.129
Hey, Miss Lane.

00:10:04.129 --> 00:10:07.129
Looking for an ace photographer to shoot tomorrow's column one?

00:10:07.129 --> 00:10:09.129
But you camber back into pants, Wilson.

00:10:09.129 --> 00:10:12.129
I need you to make another delivery, ASAP.

00:10:12.129 --> 00:10:14.129
Name's Lois, Lois, Slane.

00:10:14.129 --> 00:10:17.570
Clark Kent.

00:10:17.570 --> 00:10:21.570
So Kent, do you always bowl women over the first time you meet them?

00:10:21.570 --> 00:10:25.009
Why, don't be so hard on me.

00:10:25.009 --> 00:10:27.009
Just found out that his old flame is doing the last tango in Paris with the French Philanthropy.

00:10:27.009 --> 00:10:29.009
Paris with a French philanthropist.

00:10:29.009 --> 00:10:30.009
It's not as bad as you think.

00:10:30.009 --> 00:10:31.009
No need to put on an act.

00:10:31.009 --> 00:10:33.009
I know all about unrequited love.

00:10:33.009 --> 00:10:37.009
I have had more heroes exit stage left than a Greek tragedy.

00:10:37.009 --> 00:10:39.009
But you know what I find helps?

00:10:39.009 --> 00:10:41.009
Talking about it.

00:10:41.009 --> 00:10:43.009
I'm going to be at O'Malley's after work, find me,

00:10:43.009 --> 00:10:45.009
and I'll buy you a cold one.

00:10:45.009 --> 00:10:48.259
Louis Lane?

00:10:48.259 --> 00:10:55.120
That's what it says on my Pulitzer.

00:10:55.120 --> 00:10:58.120
You're in possession of property belonging to the U.S. government.

00:10:58.120 --> 00:11:01.120
Come with us.

00:11:01.120 --> 00:11:02.120
Hey!

00:11:02.120 --> 00:11:04.120
Hey, what are you doing?

00:11:04.120 --> 00:11:05.120
Hello?

00:11:05.120 --> 00:11:09.360
This is official government business and doesn't concern you.

00:11:09.360 --> 00:11:10.360
Back off.

00:11:10.360 --> 00:11:26.820
What just happened?

00:11:26.820 --> 00:11:28.820
Not sure, but if the head of the DDS makes a house call,

00:11:28.820 --> 00:11:29.820
it's got to be something serious.

00:11:29.820 --> 00:11:30.820
DDS?

00:11:30.820 --> 00:11:32.820
C-SPAN much, the Department of Domestic Security?

00:11:32.820 --> 00:11:35.820
That was Linda Danvers. She was appointed last month.

00:11:35.820 --> 00:11:36.820
Who would appoint her?

00:11:36.820 --> 00:11:37.820
The only person who can't.

00:11:37.820 --> 00:11:54.799
President in the United States.

00:11:54.799 --> 00:11:57.799
I still can't believe that Lex Luther was elected president.

00:11:57.799 --> 00:12:01.799
Hey, played the fear card, got the most votes, and a civic class.

00:12:01.799 --> 00:12:03.799
Ever since he branded it the Meteor Freaks,

00:12:03.799 --> 00:12:04.799
he's been a national hero.

00:12:04.799 --> 00:12:06.799
Meteor freaks, there was still a meteor shower?

00:12:06.799 --> 00:12:10.799
Uh, yeah, made headlines coast to coast. Luther saved the day.

00:12:10.799 --> 00:12:12.799
Because Lois's arrest have anything to do with Lex.

00:12:12.799 --> 00:12:14.799
Oh, so now you're on a first-name basis with the president?

00:12:14.799 --> 00:12:15.799
I just know he can be dangerous.

00:12:15.799 --> 00:12:17.799
Lois is a friend of mine. I don't want to see her get hurt.

00:12:17.799 --> 00:12:19.799
Look, aren't you sipping the poison a little quick there, Romeo?

00:12:19.799 --> 00:12:21.799
You two just met.

00:12:21.799 --> 00:12:22.799
There must be some way we can help her.

00:12:22.799 --> 00:12:25.799
Look, I'm just trying to keep my own butt out of an orange jumpsuit.

00:12:25.799 --> 00:12:29.080
Tell me where they took her.

00:12:29.080 --> 00:12:33.080
I only know she dropped this mess in my lap, and I got a clean house before Big Brother comes knocking.

00:12:34.080 --> 00:12:35.080
Hey, give me that back.

00:12:35.080 --> 00:12:38.080
What do you think that you're doing?

00:12:38.080 --> 00:12:40.080
What does this mean?

00:12:40.080 --> 00:12:42.080
I'm just a messenger.

00:12:42.080 --> 00:12:45.080
Lois doesn't like courier services, so I make her deliveries.

00:12:45.080 --> 00:12:47.080
Where were you taking it?

00:12:47.080 --> 00:12:51.080
I guess you didn't get the memo that said, why should I tell you?

00:12:51.080 --> 00:12:56.879
That's a good answer.

00:12:56.879 --> 00:12:58.879
It's ace of clubs.

00:12:58.879 --> 00:13:01.879
Look for the suit at the end of the bar. That's all I know.

00:13:01.879 --> 00:13:24.649
Your messenger days are over.

00:13:24.649 --> 00:13:35.149
Sheriff Adams?

00:13:35.149 --> 00:13:37.149
Adams?

00:13:37.149 --> 00:13:41.399
A long time since anyone's called me by that handle.

00:13:41.399 --> 00:13:42.399
Do I know you?

00:13:42.399 --> 00:13:44.399
I grew up in Smallville.

00:13:44.399 --> 00:13:48.399
I kicked that town's dust off my boots a long time ago.

00:13:48.399 --> 00:13:51.399
What's your business here?

00:13:51.399 --> 00:13:55.120
I'm making a delivery.

00:13:55.120 --> 00:13:57.120
Why the hell is this open?

00:13:57.120 --> 00:13:59.120
I want to know what's going on.

00:13:59.120 --> 00:14:02.120
Our Lois Lane won't be the only one in trouble with the government.

00:14:02.120 --> 00:14:06.080
You're out of your league here, Slim.

00:14:06.080 --> 00:14:08.080
I am the government.

00:14:08.080 --> 00:14:09.080
No, get back to Smallville before.

00:14:09.080 --> 00:14:12.080
to Smallville before I lose my ladylike charm

00:14:12.080 --> 00:14:14.080
and arrest your hide.

00:14:14.080 --> 00:14:16.080
You mean like you did to Lois Lane?

00:14:16.080 --> 00:14:20.960
Lane was arrested.

00:14:20.960 --> 00:14:23.960
Don't I so surprised the DDS picked her up this morning.

00:14:23.960 --> 00:14:26.960
Look, the DDS said that Lois was in possession

00:14:26.960 --> 00:14:28.960
of something that belonged to the government.

00:14:28.960 --> 00:14:34.090
Whatever it was came from you, didn't it?

00:14:34.090 --> 00:14:36.090
You're her informant.

00:14:36.090 --> 00:14:39.500
If anyone hears about this,

00:14:39.500 --> 00:14:43.500
I will hunt you down like a henhouse fox.

00:14:43.500 --> 00:14:44.500
Do you hear me?

00:14:44.500 --> 00:14:45.500
I only want to help.

00:14:45.500 --> 00:14:46.500
Tell me.

00:14:46.500 --> 00:14:48.500
She is.

00:14:48.500 --> 00:14:51.500
If the department picked her up, no one can help her now.

00:14:51.500 --> 00:14:53.500
Not even me.

00:14:53.500 --> 00:14:54.500
Just let me try.

00:14:54.500 --> 00:14:56.500
Don't bother.

00:14:56.500 --> 00:15:00.960
Just give it up.

00:15:00.960 --> 00:15:01.960
I don't give up.

00:15:01.960 --> 00:15:05.309
Tell me where I can find Lois Lane.

00:15:05.309 --> 00:15:17.320
Bring her inside and lock her up.

00:15:17.320 --> 00:15:19.320
Don't let anyone talk to her until I return.

00:15:19.320 --> 00:15:20.320
Ms. Move.

00:15:20.320 --> 00:15:22.320
Don't touch me.

00:15:22.320 --> 00:15:26.320
What is this place?

00:15:26.320 --> 00:15:44.139
You okay?

00:15:44.139 --> 00:15:45.139
You okay?

00:15:45.139 --> 00:15:46.139
Yeah.

00:15:46.139 --> 00:16:07.830
Talk about sweeping a girl off her feet.

00:16:07.830 --> 00:16:09.830
Andy having a meteor freak on my side?

00:16:09.830 --> 00:16:10.830
Not a meteor freak.

00:16:10.830 --> 00:16:11.830
Right.

00:16:11.830 --> 00:16:17.830
It may be a mess, but I thought Olson's loft is the last place Luther's stormtroopers would come looking for us.

00:16:17.830 --> 00:16:19.830
You might tell me why you're public enemy number one?

00:16:19.830 --> 00:16:20.830
I'm not.

00:16:20.830 --> 00:16:24.830
I happen to have a highly classified document that proves Luther is putting the country in jeopardy.

00:16:24.830 --> 00:16:26.830
Look at this.

00:16:26.830 --> 00:16:32.830
Satellite images have revealed that our enemy has deployed nuclear missiles within striking distance of our country.

00:16:32.830 --> 00:16:33.830
My fellow.

00:16:33.830 --> 00:16:35.830
Americans.

00:16:35.830 --> 00:16:38.830
A threat in our own backyard will not be tolerated.

00:16:38.830 --> 00:16:42.830
This hostile action leaves us no option but to answer with force.

00:16:42.830 --> 00:16:45.830
One little problem.

00:16:45.830 --> 00:16:48.830
The threat is as phony as my uncle's hairpiece.

00:16:48.830 --> 00:16:52.779
The missiles don't exist.

00:16:52.779 --> 00:16:54.779
There's no surprise that Lex would lie.

00:16:54.779 --> 00:16:57.779
Why would he create a national crisis that wasn't there?

00:16:57.779 --> 00:17:01.779
While the DDS was chauffeering me to my inquisition,

00:17:01.779 --> 00:17:04.779
I overheard an agent saying they were taking the eagle to the mountaintop.

00:17:04.779 --> 00:17:06.779
Sounds like some kind of code.

00:17:06.779 --> 00:17:09.779
It means they're moving Luther to the NORAD bunker.

00:17:09.779 --> 00:17:13.779
They would only do that for one reason. Nuclear war.

00:17:13.779 --> 00:17:19.279
And since the threat is fake, it means he wants to give the enemy a sucker punch

00:17:19.279 --> 00:17:22.279
with a preemptive nuclear strike.

00:17:22.279 --> 00:17:26.279
I need to post the truth on the planet's front page before Luther presses the button.

00:17:26.279 --> 00:17:30.279
But if Lex goes through with this strike, he's got to know that each side will destroy the other.

00:17:30.279 --> 00:17:33.279
That's what I don't understand. Luther's not suicidal.

00:17:33.279 --> 00:17:35.279
Why would he want to hit Earth's delete key?

00:17:35.279 --> 00:17:41.920
elite key.

00:17:41.920 --> 00:17:42.920
Is it him?

00:17:42.920 --> 00:17:45.920
Milton Fine, the chief of staff?

00:17:45.920 --> 00:17:49.920
He's powerful, but we're not talking nuclear bomb powerful.

00:17:49.920 --> 00:17:51.920
So he managed to get here.

00:17:51.920 --> 00:17:53.920
What are you talking about?

00:17:53.920 --> 00:17:55.920
He's behind it all, Lois.

00:17:55.920 --> 00:17:57.920
Milton Fine doesn't care what happens to this planet.

00:17:57.920 --> 00:17:59.920
Because he's not human.

00:17:59.920 --> 00:18:07.769
He's a machine.

00:18:07.769 --> 00:18:09.769
He might come across a little stiff on Lerick King,

00:18:09.769 --> 00:18:11.769
but you're saying he's an android?

00:18:11.769 --> 00:18:13.769
If I was here to take him on, none of this would have happened.

00:18:13.769 --> 00:18:15.769
I thought everything would be better off if I wasn't involved,

00:18:15.769 --> 00:18:18.769
I wasn't involved, but it turns out it's worse than I ever imagined.

00:18:18.769 --> 00:18:19.769
I don't understand.

00:18:19.769 --> 00:18:26.859
How does any of this have anything to do with you?

00:18:26.859 --> 00:18:28.859
You're an android, aren't you?

00:18:28.859 --> 00:18:30.859
I'm the one person who can defeat fine.

00:18:30.859 --> 00:18:35.160
I need you to trust me.

00:18:35.160 --> 00:18:43.250
Luther's holding a press conference in Smallville in 20 minutes.

00:18:43.250 --> 00:18:46.250
The only way to stop his plan is to get to the briefcase

00:18:46.250 --> 00:18:48.250
with the nuclear attack codes.

00:18:48.250 --> 00:18:50.250
If I destroy it, then he can't initiate the launch.

00:18:50.250 --> 00:18:53.250
They guard that nuclear football better than the Hope Diamond.

00:18:53.250 --> 00:18:55.250
I'll get past security.

00:18:55.250 --> 00:18:56.250
Wait.

00:18:56.250 --> 00:18:58.250
Even if you white tornadoes,

00:18:58.250 --> 00:19:01.250
you weigh in there, you're still going to stick out like a red and blue thumb.

00:19:01.250 --> 00:19:09.490
You need to blend in.

00:19:09.490 --> 00:19:11.490
Olsen's roommates about the right size.

00:19:11.490 --> 00:19:13.490
Lois, we don't have time for this.

00:19:13.490 --> 00:19:15.490
Then stop standing around. Strip.

00:19:15.490 --> 00:19:23.319
All right.

00:19:23.319 --> 00:19:26.319
Kent, this is no time to be modest. Armageddon's minutes away.

00:19:26.319 --> 00:19:43.359
Well done. Here, put this on.

00:19:43.359 --> 00:19:49.589
Lois Lane.

00:19:49.589 --> 00:19:52.589
If anyone asks, it's a typo. Your name's Lewis.

00:19:52.589 --> 00:20:00.000
What's wrong now?

00:20:00.000 --> 00:20:01.000
Something's missing.

00:20:01.000 --> 00:20:08.339
Yeah, I think I should have this.

00:20:09.339 --> 00:20:24.339
Considering your extraordinary abilities, it's hard to believe Miss Lane escaped for me.

00:20:24.339 --> 00:20:27.339
Unless perhaps you wanted it to.

00:20:27.339 --> 00:20:30.339
After all the years we've been together, you turn on me now.

00:20:30.339 --> 00:20:32.339
You're like my brother, Lex.

00:20:32.339 --> 00:20:34.339
You know I'll always be loyal to you.

00:20:34.339 --> 00:20:37.339
Letting my enemies escape is an odd way of showing it.

00:20:37.339 --> 00:20:38.339
You don't know your true enemy.

00:20:38.339 --> 00:20:39.339
His enemy.

00:20:39.339 --> 00:20:40.339
is Milton fine.

00:20:40.339 --> 00:20:50.230
My closest advisor, the man who got me elected.

00:20:50.230 --> 00:20:52.230
He didn't do it alone.

00:20:52.230 --> 00:20:56.230
